<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.Automation</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.Automation</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Automation Platform Foundation (Phase B23). The orchestration layer the frontend's Phase 18
      register found no contract behind: an automation registry, an execution engine over the
      platform's existing integration-event stream, a durable timezone-correct occurrence store,
      execution history, a server-evaluated capability set, a dry run that performs nothing, reminders,
      saved searches, an audience estimator and an audit trail.

      What this module owns: the fact that a member, a community or an organization configured a rule;
      which trigger it watches; which conditions it applies; which allow-listed actions it asks for;
      when a time-based rule is next due; and what happened on every attempt.

      What it deliberately does not own, and never duplicates:

        Delivery is B13's. This module composes no notification, chooses no channel, sends no push and
        owns no device. It publishes AutomationNotificationRequested and stops. The channel, the
        priority, the quiet-hours decision, the digest window and the de-duplication are all B13's, and
        the run record reports what B13 answered rather than what this module assumed.

        Money is B15's. There is no action that can transfer, withdraw, credit, refund, charge or
        settle, and there is no amount or destination field anywhere in the domain model. Financial
        triggers notify about money that has already moved. An architecture test asserts the assembly
        names no financial write.

        Domain truth is the owning module's. This module stores no event, no job, no listing, no guide
        and no conversation. Every trigger is a published contract it consumes, and every condition is
        answered from that contract's payload or declared unevaluable.

        External providers are B22's. There is no HttpClient in this assembly.

        Analytics is B19's. Automation telemetry goes to B19's existing ingestion route.

        Geography is B21's. There is no second geo model.

        Resilience, leases, rate limiting, secrets and dead-lettering are B17's.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, to
      Identity, or to Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    One module reference, and it is the shape Conversations and Integrations already use.

    Notifications, for its catalogue contributor seams only — INotificationCategoryContributor,
    INotificationTemplateContributor, INotificationRuleContributor. FRONTEND-PHASE18-GAP-024 asks for
    automation-owned categories so a member can mute automation notifications separately from the
    platform's own, and the wording that renders an automation's message belongs with the module that
    knows what an automation is.

    Notably absent: every vertical whose events this module consumes. A consumer needs the published
    contract in Diaspora.Contracts and nothing else, which is the whole point of publishing one.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Persistence\Diaspora.Persistence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Notifications\Diaspora.Modules.Notifications.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
